  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "The Scoped Ledger",
    "overview": "**Creative North Star: \"The Scoped Ledger\"**\n\nKairo looks like the operational ledger it replaces, cleaned up and given a lock. A slate-900 ink column (the sidebar, and on the landing page the whole hero stage) holds white task tables whose meaning is carried by small tinted pills: status, priority, scope. One indigo carries every commitment the user can make: the active nav item, the primary button, the selected viewer, the focus ring. Everything else is slate.\n\nDensity is high and calm. Working surfaces run on 12px text, 10–11px uppercase column labels and tabular numerals so dates, counts and IDs line up like a spreadsheet. The marketing surface is the same world at page scale: the real shell (sidebar, top bar, task table) becomes the hero instead of a screenshot, with display type in tight-tracked Inter bold above it. Depth comes from hairline borders and the ink/paper contrast, not from shadows; only things that float above the workspace (drawer, modal card, the hero stage) lift.\n\nThe world rejects gradients and glass on new surfaces. The app's earlier indigo-to-purple gradients were removed; the indigo is flat.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "Slate-900 ink ground against white and cool-paper task surfaces.",
      "One committed accent (indigo-600); semantic tints for state, never for decoration.",
      "Inter throughout, tabular numerals for every count, date and ID.",
      "Hairline-bordered panels at 12px radius; pills at 6px.",
      "Product truth as imagery: the real shell, real seed rows, real API responses in mono."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The One Commitment Rule",
        "body": "Indigo appears only where the user commits or is located: a primary action, the current nav item, the selected scope, focus. If an element is not clickable-and-primary or currently selected, it is not indigo-600.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Tint-Means-State Rule",
        "body": "Emerald, rose, amber, blue and violet appear as 50-wash + 700-text pairs bound to a fixed meaning (Excel/done, blocked/urgent/error, high/held back, in progress/medium, in review). They are never used as section colour or ornament.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Tabular Rule",
        "body": "Every count, date, row number and ID uses tabular numerals (the `.tabular` utility, `font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums`). Columns of numbers must align like the spreadsheet they replace.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Uppercase-Is-Structure Rule",
        "body": "Uppercase tracked labels are reserved for structural captions (column headers, nav group headings, form field labels). Section headings on marketing surfaces carry no eyebrow above them.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Stable Stage Rule",
        "body": "Interactive demos reserve their full height. When content collapses (the viewer switch hiding rows), the frame keeps its size and the vacated space carries an explanatory note, so the page never shifts under the reader.",
        "section": "layout"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Border-First Rule",
        "body": "A panel that sits in the page flow gets a hairline border, not a shadow. Lift is earned by floating (drawer, modal, stage).",
        "section": "elevation"
      }
    ],
    "dos": [
      "**Do** keep indigo-600 for primary actions, current location, selected scope and focus only.",
      "**Do** express task state with 50-wash + 700-text pills using the fixed mapping: blue in progress, violet in review, rose blocked/urgent, amber high, emerald completed, slate backlog/to do/low.",
      "**Do** set every count, date and ID in tabular numerals, and IDs, paths and API responses in mono.",
      "**Do** separate in-flow panels with a 1px slate-200 border at 12px radius; reserve shadows for drawers, modals and the hero stage.",
      "**Do** show the real product (shell, seed rows, import preview, API probe) as imagery on marketing surfaces.",
      "**Do** transition colour only (`transition-colors`, 150–200ms) on hover; use `cubic-bezier(0.16, 1, 0.3, 1)` for entrances, and honour `prefers-reduced-motion`.",
      "**Do** reserve the full height of interactive demos so toggling never shifts the page."
    ],
    "donts": [
      "**Don't** use gradients anywhere; the indigo-to-purple gradients were removed and stay removed.",
      "**Don't** add glass (translucent blurred) panels to new surfaces; the sticky top bar's white/90 blur is the only incumbent case.",
      "**Don't** introduce a second accent or use purple for roles or emphasis; indigo is the brand and violet means \"In Review\" only.",
      "**Don't** put eyebrow labels above section headings or invent metrics, customers or testimonials as decoration.",
